<item>
            <title>[LU-20829] sanity test_230x: migrate should-fail race allows migrate to succeed</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20829</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;test_230x sets osp.&amp;lt;mdt&amp;gt;-osp-MDT0001.reserved_ino_low above the current free inode count, sets maxage=1, sleeps 4s, then expects &apos;lfs migrate -m 1 -c $MDSCOUNT $dir&apos; to fail with ENOSPC. In session c00789de-74d3-46d4-8a74-ba438fd25928 (test set f24423b5-03cd-4e60-b535-51bb4c8bd37d), the review-dne-zfs-subtest-change job, which repeats a patch&apos;s changed subtests back to back, ran test_230x 57 times: it passed 56 times (migrate correctly failed with &apos;No space left on device (28)&apos;) and failed once on repeat 57 with &apos;migrate d230x.sanity should fail&apos;. The osp.lustre-MDT0000-osp-MDT0001.* get_param/set_param calls resolved identically on every repeat, so this is not a parameter-resolution problem; it is a race where the OSP&apos;s cached free-inode statfs data (refreshed via maxage=1) had not picked up the lowered reserved_ino_low within the fixed 4s sleep before the migrate ran, letting it succeed when it should not have.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Not caused by the patch under test (change 56384): its only edit to test_230x renames the mdt_name lookup (mdtname_from_index -&amp;gt; ${MDT&lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;0&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;}) and drops a redundant leading glob from the osp.* parameter path; the reserved_ino_low/maxage/sleep timing this race depends on is unchanged from before the patch. maloo test-history shows 93 test_230x occurrences across 30 lustre-reviews sessions in the last 30 days with only this one failure &amp;#8211; ordinary single-run review jobs rarely catch a roughly 1.8% timing flake, and this repeat-testing job type is what exposed it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Raised by Patch Watcher run pw-engineer-56384-ps35-0a28a92cf5bf on &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/56384&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/56384&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
